{"title":"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#The_Simple_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Simple Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Quick_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quick Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Incredible Hulk can double the distance he jumps with each succeeding jump. If his first jump is 1 meter, the second jump is 2 meters, the third jump is 4 meters, and so on, then on which jump will he first be able to jump more than 1 kilometer (1,000 meters)?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654d606cc73323a6e7ecb203c5b33c0ba73c9c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9^\\text{th} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 10^\\text{th} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 11^\\text{th} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 12^\\text{th} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 13^\\text{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"451\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a geometric sequence in which the common ratio is 2. To find the jump that would be over a 1000 meters, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/50811f350197d47b2ddb684f3b7d07ce96a0bdca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}=1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>However, because the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3688876ff545b6900b80c429336386b50e4a4326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> and not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac77a5bfa42cfdff2a0fea269dab35c205b7d14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1=2$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, the solution to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd19b64c2dfb06a98d73d33a2f7857f3a16981b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-0+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 11^{\\text{th}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"182\" height=\"31\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ifw2RXsqNwc\">https://youtu.be/Ifw2RXsqNwc</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Simple_Solution\">The Simple Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: The Simple Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you don't want to use your brain and wishes to use the easiest solution, here's it. We must list all the numbers times 2;\n</p><p>1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024.\n</p><p>Since 1024 is larger than 1000, now we just have to count the numbers. There are 11, thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097428c77fa5f267fd6bf975dfa6aeaf5a84031a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 11^{\\text{th}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"79\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quick_Solution\">Quick Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Quick Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You could just know that the first multiple of 2 that goes over 1000 meters (1 km)would be 1024 so the answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097428c77fa5f267fd6bf975dfa6aeaf5a84031a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 11^{\\text{th}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"79\" height=\"33\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e06599c07f5b758ccb7072235380e6f6d01aa0eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{\\text{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is already known.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8\">2013 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 A